<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Awraba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Awraba were a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> tribal confederation of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. In the 7th century their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kusaila">Kusaila</a>, a Christian, led resistance to the Arab conquest and defeated and killed the Arab commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uqba-ibn-nafi">Uqba ibn Nafi</a> in 683. Later Muslim and settled around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volubilis">Volubilis</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, in 788 they welcomed the Alid refugee Idris I and recognised him as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a>, founding the Idrisid state.</p></div>
